  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The length of a metallic wire is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and its area of cross-section is reduced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>.</mo></math> The percentage change in resistance of the metallic wire is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given data is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>A</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>96</mn><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>Using the formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;the new&nbsp;resistance is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>96</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the percentage increase is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
